# The guard of a passed test for a present element proves that this position of this array holds an element: to a read of a present element, which then needs nothing of the prototypes, and to an access inside the length. The test of the bounds proves no element, because a position inside the length may hold a hole. The test read the element, so its proof ends where an element of an array that may be this one is written. The guard of a passed test for a position inside a view lasts until the view may change its length. Each function named bad is refused for one reason, and differs in it from a function named good
# FORM: Prepared
# RUN: verify
# DIAGNOSTIC: InvalidGuard 9
# DIAGNOSTIC: GuardNotAvailable 4

module m0 path="main.js" displayPath="main.js"
function f0 name="goodPresentRead" parameters=[{type=Array<number>}, {type=number}] results=[{type=anything}] {
    v2 = HasArrayStorage v0 arrayStorage=Double
    Branch v2 -> taken b1(| 0), notTaken b3()
  b1(v3):
    v4 = IsElementPresent v0, v1, v3 arrayStorage=Double
    Branch v4 -> taken b2(| 0), notTaken b3()
  b2(v5):
    v6 = AllGuards v3, v5
    v7 = GetArrayElement v0, v1, v6 arrayStorage=Double level=Expected [isPresent]
    Return v7
  b3():
    v8 = Undefined
    Return v8
}
